<title>SPAIN: Spain 1-year bill yield sets new low of 6.480 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain 1-year bill yield sets new low of 6.480 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain announced the following results at Wednesday's Treasury debt auction (amounts bid, allocated in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p>ISSUE	Yield    Pvs     Price     Pvs	Bid    Allocated</p>
<p>1-year     6.480    6.508   93.85    93.81    714.01  285.23</p>
<p>NOTE - This yield sets a new record low. Previous was set at 6.503 percent on October 16, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
